<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emílio Garrastazu Médici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1905–1985</span> · Also known as Médici</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emílio Garrastazu Médici was a Brazilian general who served as president from 1969 to 1974, the harshest period of the military dictatorship. His government used censorship, torture and killings to destroy the armed left, while the 'Brazilian miracle' brought very rapid economic growth and great public works such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trans-amazonian-highway">Trans-Amazonian Highway</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emilio-garrastazu-medici.jpg" alt="Emílio Garrastazu Médici" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Em%C3%ADlio_Garrastazu_M%C3%A9dici,_presidente_da_Rep%C3%BAblica._(cropped)(2).tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
